! Mining software repository with Pharo

Nicolas Hlad  (nicolas.hlad@berger-levrault.com)

""Abstract:""
Git platforms like GitLab, GitHub, and Bitbucket offer valuable insights into team dynamics and project workflows. 
In this regards, the field of Mining Software Repositories (MSR) works on techniques and tools to extract and analyze these data. 

This presentation introduces GitProjectHealth (GPH), an framework to interact with Git platforms and analyze them. 
We build GPH leveraging Moose metamodel platform to build an extensible metamodel of a Git platform. 
Futhermore, we leverage the metamodel extension mecanism to connect Git platform and other social platform model, sush as Jira (ticket management).

This talk develop 3 aspects of GPH: first, its ability to analyze open-source repository; second, its build-in metrics; and finaly, its metamodel connection demonstrat with Jira. 

""Bio:""
Nicolas Hlad is a PhD computer scientist at Berger-Levrault, France. He conducted his Phd in 2022, working on software product lines. 
Since then, he focusing of software static analyse using metamodel technology built-in Pharo, and on how Generative Artificial Intelligence (GenAI) sush 
as Large Language Model (LLM) can impact the work of developers. Recently, he used MSR as a mean to analyse the developer's activity when they benefits 
from GenAI LLM tools in their workflow. 
